[
  {
    "stepId": "binomial-center",
    "id": "binomial-center",
    "claimId": "thm:rate-adaptive-center",
    "purpose": "Orient the sign-comparison machinery.",
    "explanation": "The binomial-center theorem states positivity domains for the comparison gap. The manuscript then derives the low-rate boundary through a hinge-transform argument, and handles the zero-center sign by reflection. These are supporting statements for the main finite comparison, not additional assumptions needed to read its headline conclusion. Matching the exposition to the supplied signatures regroups the trace average as a binomial count and identifies \u03b8 and a positive scale. The symmetric zero-center identity is separate from the conventional strict average-only endpoint argument.",
